================================================================================
SCOPE OF THE APACHE-2.0 GRANT
================================================================================

Every source file in this repository was authored by us, so the Apache-2.0
licence in LICENSE covers all of it. No third-party source file is vendored
here: the pipeline is built entirely on nnU-Net v2 as an installed dependency,
and nothing in this repository imports the organizers' baseline.

The organizer baseline is therefore NOT redistributed:

    https://github.com/qutaiping/CMR_multi_baseline
    commit cfc38fe0bd9c3d9b17100f9fee51b6520361979e

It is referenced only because its reference LVEF routine (3D_seg/
calculate_lv_ef.py, read_id_slice_sax) establishes that the cine-SAX
phase-count metadata file this pipeline looks for is part of the released data
contract. Upstream publishes no LICENSE file; obtain terms from its authors.

================================================================================
UPSTREAM MODELS AND DATA
================================================================================

No model weights and no challenge data are distributed in this repository.

- CMR-MULTI 2026 challenge data, released by the organizers under CC BY
  (Attribution) at https://huggingface.co/datasets/TaipingQu/CMR-MULTI. Pinned
  to commit cfdbfec4b18b245bd96b631b5b330236ae2f238e; see TRAINING.md.
  Not redistributed. CC BY attaches an attribution requirement, not a
  non-commercial one, so checkpoints trained on it carry no non-commercial
  restriction from the data — attribute the organizers if you distribute them.

- No pretrained model weights are used. Every network in the submitted system
  is trained from random initialization by nnU-Net v2; the container downloads
  nothing at runtime and runs fully offline.

- Built on nnU-Net v2 (Apache-2.0), PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), NumPy / SciPy /
  pandas (BSD-3-Clause), nibabel (MIT), SimpleITK (Apache-2.0), scikit-image
  (BSD-3-Clause), batchgenerators (Apache-2.0), dynamic-network-architectures
  (Apache-2.0), einops (MIT). Exact pins are in docker/requirements.txt.

